Package: ristools
Title: R package for working RIS files, prioritising simplicity and transparency
Version: 1.0.1
Authors@R:
    person("Mark", "Engelbert", email = "mengelbert@3ieimpact.org",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Reads and writes RIS files with minimal "interpretation". A RIS file becomes a data frame whose columns are the file's own tags, so it can be inspected, edited and written back with nothing renamed, merged or reordered. Multiple values in a single field (authors, keywords, JEL descriptors, ISSNs) are joined with a delimiter ( | ) that rarely appears in real data, making the conversion reversible. OpenAlex works can be read from JSON into the same flat data frame and written out as RIS.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Imports:
    jsonlite,
    stats
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
